		"notes": {
			"techniques": "Chilies and Sichuan pepper are bloomed in oil first, so the oil carries their aroma. The sauce is mixed in advance and added in one go.",
			"chemistry": "The cornstarch coating protects the chicken from drying out (velveting) and helps the sauce cling. Sichuan pepper contains hydroxy-alpha-sanshool, which causes the tingling numbness.",
			"spiceProfile": "Hot, numbing and tangy-sweet, the Sichuan \"lychee\" flavour of balanced vinegar and sugar.",
			"variations": "The Sichuan original has no vegetables apart from scallions and a small amount of glossy sauce. American takeout versions add peppers and courgette and more, sweeter sauce."
